.el .ds Aq '
.TH byssus-dry-run 8  "byssus 0.1.0" "Byssus Manual"
.SH NAME
byssus\-dry\-run \- Validate configuration, kernel, permissions and propagation, and show what a reconcile would do, without mounting anything
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbyssus dry\-run\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate configuration, kernel, permissions and propagation, and show what a reconcile would do, without mounting anything.
.PP
When run as root with a service user configured, checks run as that user. Exits 1 if any check fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Main configuration file [default: /etc/byssus/byssus.toml]
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Drop\-in configuration directory [default: /etc/byssus/conf.d]
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Log level for diagnostics on stderr: error, warn, info, debug, trace
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
